<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's BES wants to expand abroad.</title>
<headline>Portugal's BES wants to expand abroad.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's third biggest private bank Banco Espirito Santo is seeking opportunities to expand operations in Brazil, South Africa, Angola and Mozambique, its president Ricardo Espirito Santo Salgado said.</p>
<p>He told Reuters BES was considering buying a retail bank at a regional level in Brazil and was also seeking opportunities in South Africa as well as the former Portuguese colonies of Angola and Mozambique.</p>
<p>&quot;We want to boost the internationalisation of BES,&quot; he said after announcing a 21.3 percent year-on-year increase in 1996 profits to 23.593 billion escudos.</p>
<p>-- Sergio Goncalves, Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
